---
description: Commit-bound verification, staleness and final release rules
alwaysApply: true
---

- `movie_muse_build_status.yaml` is the only completion ledger; `dependency_dag.yaml` is the only work-package graph.
- A package is runnable only when every dependency is current PASS.
- PASS requires committed code, exact commands, evidence, fingerprint, UTC time and independent verifier PASS.
- Map every relevant change to scope keys; mark affected PASS items STALE and recursively stale every dependent.
- Reverting a change never restores PASS; rerun verification.
- A mock can satisfy deterministic contract tests but never a required live/sandbox gate.
- A skipped/quarantined/missing required check fails verification.
- The independent verifier must not be the implementer and must reproduce on a clean environment.
- `./scripts/verify_all.sh` is fail-closed and may print the exact PASS sentinel only after total success.
- Do not edit status to hide a failure or blocker. Record root cause, evidence and next action.

